  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Radioactive nuclide A can decay by two different routes as shown below.</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n\n<p>D and H are the final decay products, B, C, F, and G are intermediate products. Which one of the following statements is correct?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\">C and G have the same mass number.</li>\n<li data-label=\"B\">The nucleon number of B is the same as the nucleon number of G.</li>\n<li data-label=\"C\">C and G are different isotopes of the same element.</li>\n<li data-label=\"D\">B and F have different atomic numbers.</li>\n</ol>"
  },
